#: ../../../AArch64SME.md:425
msgid "AArch64 Predicate-as-Counter Type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AArch64SME.md:427
msgid "**Overview:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AArch64SME.md:429
msgid ""
"The predicate-as-counter type represents the type of a predicate-as-counter "
"value held in an AArch64 SVE predicate register. Such a value contains "
"information about the number of active lanes, the element width and a bit "
"that indicates whether the generated mask should be inverted. ACLE "
"intrinsics should be used to move the predicate-as-counter value to/from a "
"predicate vector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AArch64SME.md:435
msgid "There are certain limitations on the type:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AArch64SME.md:437
msgid "The type can be used for function parameters and return values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AArch64SME.md:438
msgid ""
"The supported LLVM operations on this type are limited to `load`, `store`, "
"`phi`, `select`, and `alloca` instructions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../AArch64SME.md:441
msgid "The predicate-as-counter type is a scalable type."
msgstr ""

